      "side": 1,
      "message": "TIt seems really strange to use \"tests\" to perform functions that are effectively test environment setup. For example:\n- If you run the test out of order things won\u0027t work.\n- Running only some tests but not others will fail, or may leave the device in a bad state, because each test does not clean up after itself.\n\nIt\u0027s also inconsistent with what other tests do (e.g., the VPN tests).\n\nI think it would be better to design as follows:\n- Have the tests only run in one APK (.app?), and use the other APK (.app2?) as a helper APK, that is only used to check \"what things look like from another UID\"\n- Have this file run two tests, one where the callback is created in the test app (which tests that the SoftApConfig is visible) and one where the callback is created in the helper app (which tests that the SoftApConfig is null)\n- Use an AIDL interface to let the test APK ask the helper APK \"tell me what TetheringInterface you got from the callback\".\n\nThis test should probably be moved to another CL, this CL is large enough already.",
      "revId": "76bb5218674d69b90867c7adb3a9e1a24a85821e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
